  "description": "The certificate in speech and hearing foundations provides postbaccalaureate students from other disciplines the necessary prerequisite course work in speech-language pathology and audiology to apply to graduate programs in speech-language pathology. The certificate consists of six courses. Students planning to apply to a master's program in speech-language pathology are also required to complete one course each in biology, physics or chemistry, statistics, and social sciences.",
